WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:08.560
In nineteen sixty-two, your Congress decided that after proving a drug won't kill you, sick people should wait another eight

2
00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:14.440
point two years before they're allowed to take it. The drug passed safety testing.

3
00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:18.760
It won't kill you, won't melt your liver, won't make your hair migrate to your back.

4
00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:27.060
But you can't have it, because a committee needs to spend eight point two years making sure it works well enough.

5
00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:33.100
You're not allowed to volunteer for the trials that would answer that question faster, either.

6
00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:37.020
You are, however, allowed to die. This was called "safety."

7
00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:45.560
On Wishonia, when we confirm something won't harm you (no organ damage, no mutations, no growing a second head), we let

8
00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:49.180
you try it. On Earth, you lock it in a cabinet and form a committee.

9
00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:54.020
The committee meets quarterly. You decompose on a different schedule.

10
00:00:55.160 --> 00:01:02.520
Then, during those eight point two years of efficacy testing, the drugs are tested on three thousand young, healthy volunteers

11
00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:06.790
(excluding the sick, elderly, and anyone on other medications).

12
00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:12.820
The very people dying from the disease are banned from the trials testing treatments for their disease.

13
00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:21.200
When the drug is finally approved, it's prescribed to millions of actual sick people, where the problems finally show up.

14
00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:27.440
It's like testing sunscreen on people who live in caves, then acting surprised when it fails outdoors.

15
00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:37.920
A Note on Blame. When this chapter says "the F.D.A. does X," read it as "the nineteen sixty-two law requires the F.D.A.

16
00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:42.760
to do X." Congress wrote the rules. The F.D.A. follows them.

17
00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:49.680
Blaming the F.D.A. is like blaming the gun instead of the person who loaded it, aimed it at patients, and pulled the trigger

18
00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:58.800
on a sixty-two-year schedule. "But What About Safety?". This is the part where humans panic, so let me be very precise about

19
00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:04.960
what this chapter is (and isn't) proposing. Keep: Phase One safety testing.

20
00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:13.100
It screens for death, organ damage, toxic reactions, dangerous side effects, and all the creative ways a molecule can ruin

21
00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:18.400
a human body. It works. It caught thalidomide. It takes two point three years.

22
00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:24.180
Nobody is suggesting you skip it. Keep (but fix): efficacy testing.

23
00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:32.640
You should do massively more of it. But open it to every patient who wants to participate, publish all results (positive

24
00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:38.260
AND negative), and stop blocking access to known-safe drugs while you run the trials.

25
00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:47.080
Remove: The part where known-safe drugs sit in a cabinet for eight point two years while dying patients are banned from

26
00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:56.380
trying them and banned from the trials testing them. To be excruciatingly clear: this chapter is not arguing against efficacy

27
00:02:56.380 --> 00:03:05.120
testing. It is arguing for radically more efficacy testing, on real patients, with transparent results, while not holding

28
00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:12.880
known-safe drugs hostage during the process. On Wishonia, we have a word for "preventing someone from accessing a substance

29
00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:18.040
confirmed not to harm them while they die from the condition it might treat."

30
00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:26.540
The word is "murder." You call it "the approval process." The forty-four point one times Inefficiency Tax.

31
00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:35.060
Compare two real-world systems for testing drugs: The Oxford RECOVERY Trial tested COVID treatments on forty-seven thousand

32
00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:42.580
patients for five hundred dollars and found a life-saving treatment in three months, like a normal species would.

33
00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:51.960
The Post-nineteen sixty-two System averages forty-one thousand dollars per trial and takes nine point one years to approve

34
00:03:51.960 --> 00:04:01.880
a new drug, like humans would. The current system costs forty-four point one times more and takes forty-two times longer.

35
00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:10.400
That's not inefficiency. That's a system performing exactly as designed, if the design goal was to kill people slowly enough

36
00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:15.280
that nobody notices. The eight point two year Efficacy Lag.

37
00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:24.400
Here's where your lifespan goes to die: Phase One (Safety Testing) takes two point three years to test if the drug harms

38
00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:32.280
people through death, organ damage, mutations, serious adverse reactions, and all the ways a molecule can ruin your day

39
00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:42.320
(this part works, keep it). Phase Two and Three (Efficacy Testing) takes eight point two years where the drug is now known

40
00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:49.940
safe, but patients can't have it while it is tested on young, healthy volunteers to see if it works better than placebo.

41
00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:58.780
The sick people who actually need the drug are excluded from the trial, and access is blocked until the committee is satisfied.

42
00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:05.680
This is where people die waiting for a drug that already passed every safety check your species invented.

43
00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:13.300
Not because efficacy testing is bad, but because you do it on the wrong people and lock everyone else out while you wait.

44
00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:22.420
The math is simple: If you die in year five and the drug that passed every safety screen gets approved in year ten, the

45
00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:31.260
regulatory process murdered you. Not hypothetically. You are dead because a committee decided that confirming efficacy was

46
00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:39.580
more important than your continued existence. That's eight point two years sitting in regulatory purgatory after we already

47
00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:44.230
know the drug won't harm you. No toxicity. No organ failure.

48
00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:49.500
No spontaneous extra limbs. The solution isn't to skip efficacy testing.

49
00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:58.000
It's to stop using it as a reason to block access. On Wishonia, when we confirm a substance is safe, we make it available

50
00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:05.820
with real-time outcome tracking so we learn if it works from the millions who take it (all of whom volunteered), not from

51
00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:12.720
three thousand hand-picked healthy people in a controlled environment that resembles no actual patient's life.

52
00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:20.240
We get MORE efficacy data, FASTER, from REAL patients, while NOBODY dies in a queue.

53
00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:29.580
You invented science yesterday, cosmically speaking. Nearly every study ends with "more research is needed," which is scientist

54
00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:33.760
for "please keep paying us while we figure out what we're looking at."

55
00:06:33.980 --> 00:06:37.940
This would be fine except people are decomposing while you figure it out.

56
00:06:38.740 --> 00:06:42.880
On Wishonia, we have a saying: "The dead have no use for data."

57
00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:49.960
You don't have that saying, which explains a lot. What the nineteen sixty-two Efficacy Requirements Changed.

58
00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:59.200
Before nineteen sixty-two, one hundred forty-four thousand physicians tested treatments on real patients and published results.

59
00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:06.180
Life expectancy grew three point eight two years every decade for eighty straight years.

60
00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:15.180
Things were going well. Naturally, Congress intervened. Phase One safety testing (added in 1938) worked perfectly.

61
00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:22.060
It screens for toxicity, organ damage, dangerous side effects, and all the ways a drug can physically harm you.

62
00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:27.240
It prevented all U.S. thalidomide deaths while Europe had thousands.

63
00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:34.800
So in 1962, Congress looked at a system that was working and thought, "What if we made this much worse?"

64
00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:43.160
They added massive pre-approval efficacy requirements via the Kefauver Harris Amendment, blocking patient access for years

65
00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:51.640
during testing. The cost of developing a drug went from twenty-four point seven million dollars to two point six billion

66
00:07:51.640 --> 00:08:00.880
dollars, a one hundred and five times increase. New drug approvals dropped from forty-six per year to thirteen, a seventy

67
00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:09.480
percent decline. Life expectancy gains slowed from three point eight two years per decade to one point five four, a sixty

68
00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:15.700
percent reduction. Time to approval stretched from two to three years to ten point five years.

69
00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:22.340
The temporal break is exact. Every metric got worse the moment the law passed.

70
00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:30.880
Like flipping a switch from "progress" to "paperwork.". The one hundred and five times cost increase is rigorously documented.

71
00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:36.919
See Drug Development Cost Analysis for methodology, sensitivity analysis, and source data.

72
00:08:37.900 --> 00:08:45.800
The Modern Consequences. Even if you think historical analysis is just opinions with footnotes, the current system's failures

73
00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:50.260
are undeniable: Scientists discover a cure for your disease.

74
00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:54.200
Phase One confirms the drug is safe (two point three years).

75
00:08:55.100 --> 00:09:01.520
You are not allowed to take the known-safe drug. You are also not allowed to join the efficacy trial (you're too sick, too

76
00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:06.380
old, or on other medications). You wait eight point two more years.

77
00:09:06.820 --> 00:09:14.160
You die. The F.D.A. approves the cure. Pharmaceutical companies charge your widow ten thousand dollars per pill.

78
00:09:15.020 --> 00:09:17.960
On Wishonia, this sequence would be considered a war crime.

79
00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:25.000
On Earth, it's called "the approval process." Beautiful system if you're a mortician or bankruptcy lawyer.

80
00:09:26.340 --> 00:09:31.460
Fourteen years from discovery to patient. That's longer than it took to build the pyramids.

81
00:09:32.220 --> 00:09:39.120
Those involved moving rocks the size of houses without machinery (also the pharaohs didn't have to file quarterly progress

82
00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:46.120
reports in triplicate). High Costs Kill Innovation, Reward Monopoly.

83
00:09:46.340 --> 00:09:53.120
Before 1962: Genius scientist invents cure, raises a few million, tests safety, gives it to people.

84
00:09:53.700 --> 00:10:01.860
Like a civilization that wants to survive would. Now: Genius scientist must convince one of three mega-corporations to spend

85
00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:06.160
two point six billion dollars on a ten percent chance of success.

86
00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:10.760
Those corporations already sell inferior drugs for the same condition.

87
00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:16.860
The math for the mega-corporation: Option One: Spend two point six billion dollars on trials.

88
00:10:17.680 --> 00:10:24.960
Ninety percent chance: Lose everything. Ten percent chance: Succeed, then cannibalize your own profitable drug.

89
00:10:25.780 --> 00:10:32.360
Option Two: Buy the patent, put it on a shelf. Zero percent chance of losing two point six billion dollars.

90
00:10:32.780 --> 00:10:36.600
One hundred percent chance your inferior cash cow keeps printing money.

91
00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:41.320
Which would you choose if you were a rational sociopath in a suit?

92
00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:45.660
The profit incentive doesn't just fail to reward better treatments.

93
00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:52.060
It actively punishes them. Off-Patent Drugs and Rare Diseases: Mathematically Doomed.

94
00:10:52.760 --> 00:11:01.520
The 1962 law made it mathematically impossible to cure diseases that aren't profitable enough: Ninety-five percent of diseases

95
00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:09.700
are rare: development costs of two point six billion dollars for a patient population of approximately ten thousand patients

96
00:11:09.700 --> 00:11:20.360
equals two hundred sixty thousand dollars per patient. No patent equals no funding: off-patent drugs can't attract billion-dollar

97
00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:29.440
investments. Pre-specification kills serendipity: one must predict what drug cures before testing.

98
00:11:30.520 --> 00:11:37.200
When something costs more, you get less of it. This is the first thing they teach in economics, and the last thing anyone

99
00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:43.240
considers when writing health policy. Ninety-five percent of diseases have zero treatments.

100
00:11:44.080 --> 00:11:48.200
Not because cures are impossible. Because cures are unprofitable.

101
00:11:49.540 --> 00:11:58.980
The Actual Death Toll of "Drug Lag". Economists call it "drug lag," which is a lovely, clinical way of saying "people rotting

102
00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:03.040
to death in a queue for drugs that have already been confirmed not to hurt them.".

103
00:12:04.180 --> 00:12:10.200
Early estimates: twenty-one thousand to one hundred twenty thousand American lives per decade.

104
00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:16.860
But that was just the U.S. A comprehensive quantitative analysis using W.H.O.

105
00:12:16.860 --> 00:12:25.600
mortality data estimates the total cost of the eight point two years post-safety efficacy delay (the lag after drugs are

106
00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:31.520
known safe): four hundred sixteen million eventually avoidable deaths.

107
00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:42.380
Including years lived with disability: seven point nine four billion disability-adjusted life years, or D.A.L.Y.s, of healthy

108
00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:53.300
human life deleted. Economic cost: one point one nine quadrillion dollars (in twenty-twenty-four U.S.D.), thirty-eight times

109
00:12:53.300 --> 00:13:01.420
more than all global pharma R. and D. spending combined. Even if these estimates are off by a factor of ten, the system

110
00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:08.760
still costs eighty-two times more per patient and takes thirty-six times longer than proven alternatives.

111
00:13:09.920 --> 00:13:17.060
Here's a news story from the Non-Existent Times by No One Ever without a picture of all the people who die from lack of

112
00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:23.140
access to life-saving treatments that might have been. Types of Error in F.D.A.

113
00:13:23.260 --> 00:13:28.960
Approval Decision If the drug is beneficial and the F.D.A. allows it, it is a correct decision.

114
00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:36.700
If the drug is harmful and the F.D.A. allows it, victims are identifiable and might appear on Oprah.

115
00:13:37.140 --> 00:13:44.060
If the drug is beneficial and the F.D.A. does not allow it, victims are not identifiable or acknowledged.

116
00:13:44.960 --> 00:13:48.600
If the drug is harmful and the F.D.A. does not allow it, it is a correct decision.

117
00:13:49.840 --> 00:13:55.500
The most infamous case: beta-blockers. Europe used them to prevent heart attacks.

118
00:13:56.380 --> 00:14:01.880
The U.S. delayed for a decade, killing an estimated one hundred thousand Americans.

119
00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:07.500
More than died in Vietnam and Korea combined. From one drug delay.

120
00:14:08.600 --> 00:14:16.450
After nineteen sixty-two, U.S. life expectancy diverged from Switzerland's (which didn't introduce the same delays).

121
00:14:16.740 --> 00:14:22.400
More drug approvals in the eighties narrowed the gap. Fewer approvals in the nineties widened it again.

122
00:14:23.580 --> 00:14:30.110
How the Incentives Work. F.D.A. Regulator Decision Tree. Approve drug that later shows problems.

123
00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:37.700
Congressional hearing (televised). "F.D.A. APPROVED KILLER DRUG" headlines.

124
00:14:38.740 --> 00:14:40.520
Career ends. Pension threatened. Delay drug that could save lives.

125
00:14:41.220 --> 00:14:44.980
Nothing happens. Dead people don't complain. Promotion on schedule.

126
00:14:45.620 --> 00:14:52.720
Retire to pharma job. This isn't conspiracy. It's just a system where the only career-ending move is doing something.

127
00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:59.540
Approve a bad drug, your name is in the newspaper. Delay a good drug, the people who could have complained are dead.

128
00:15:00.140 --> 00:15:03.480
It's a perfect incentive structure if you're optimizing for cowardice.

129
00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:13.880
The Math: Why Current Regulations Increase Total Harm. Even generously crediting ALL drug withdrawals to the 1962 changes

130
00:15:13.880 --> 00:15:22.680
(ignoring that Phase One safety testing already existed), the prevented harm totals approximately two point five nine million

131
00:15:22.680 --> 00:15:32.280
disability-adjusted life years, or D.A.L.Y.s. The delay harm totals seven point nine four billion D.A.L.Y.s.

132
00:15:33.140 --> 00:15:39.880
For every one unit of harm prevented, the current system creates three thousand and seventy units of harm through delay.

133
00:15:40.980 --> 00:15:46.100
Why Bureaucrats Are Rewarded for Letting You Die. Dr. Henry I.

134
00:15:46.160 --> 00:15:51.200
Miller ran the F.D.A. team reviewing recombinant human insulin in the early 1980s.

135
00:15:52.280 --> 00:15:57.760
Mountains of evidence showed it was safe and effective. His supervisor refused to approve it.

136
00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:03.540
If someone died from the drug, heads would roll. If people died waiting for the drug?

137
00:16:04.200 --> 00:16:08.140
Nothing happens. Dead patients don't testify before Congress.

138
00:16:09.140 --> 00:16:16.180
Clinical Trial Theater: Excluding eighty-six point one percent of Reality Makes Drugs More Dangerous.

139
00:16:17.360 --> 00:16:25.580
Here is the part I find most baffling about your species. You block dying patients from accessing known-safe drugs because

140
00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:32.580
you need to "test efficacy first." Then you ALSO block those dying patients from the efficacy trials.

141
00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:38.280
So they can't take the drug, and they can't participate in the test that would let them take the drug.

142
00:16:39.120 --> 00:16:46.120
They can, however, die. Nobody blocks that. The F.D.A. requires rigorous trials to ensure safety.

143
00:16:46.960 --> 00:16:53.560
Then it tests the drugs on people who aren't sick, aren't old, aren't on other drugs, and aren't pregnant.

144
00:16:54.420 --> 00:16:59.720
Basically, it tests drugs on triathletes and then acts surprised when grandma has a reaction.

145
00:17:01.160 --> 00:17:09.119
Trials under the current system exclude: Patients over sixty-five: Most people who actually take medications (excluded due

146
00:17:09.119 --> 00:17:14.680
to "comorbidities"). Patients under eighteen: All children (metabolism differs from adults).

147
00:17:15.500 --> 00:17:20.960
Pregnant women: Excluded entirely (then drugs prescribed during pregnancy anyway).

148
00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:26.920
Anyone with comorbidities: The sickest patients most likely to have adverse reactions.

149
00:17:27.700 --> 00:17:33.460
Anyone on other medications: Everyone elderly (can't detect drug interactions).

150
00:17:34.220 --> 00:17:37.810
Anyone too far from trial sites: Poor and rural populations.

151
00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:45.560
This is like crash-testing a car by gently rolling it into a pillow, declaring it safe, and selling it to demolition derby

152
00:17:45.560 --> 00:17:52.760
drivers. Result: In antidepressant trials alone, eighty-six point one percent of real patients are excluded.

153
00:17:53.380 --> 00:18:00.940
The drugs are tested on the healthiest people alive, declared "safe," then handed to everyone the trial specifically avoided.

154
00:18:01.960 --> 00:18:10.140
This is how Vioxx, Fen-Phen, and Bextra all got approved, celebrated, prescribed to millions, and then withdrawn after killing

155
00:18:10.140 --> 00:18:13.400
people whose demographics the trials had carefully excluded.

156
00:18:14.200 --> 00:18:17.350
The eight point two years delay didn't make these drugs safer.

157
00:18:17.860 --> 00:18:21.820
It made them seem safer by hiding the danger behind an exclusion list.

158
00:18:23.280 --> 00:18:29.080
Testing drugs only on healthy volunteers to ensure safety is like testing parachutes only on the ground.

159
00:18:30.260 --> 00:18:35.340
No Long-Term Outcome Data. Data collection can be as short as several months.

160
00:18:35.960 --> 00:18:42.780
You take the drug for forty years. Pre-Specification Requirements Kill Innovation.

161
00:18:42.800 --> 00:18:49.470
The regulations require drug developers to predict exactly what a treatment will cure before testing it on humans.

162
00:18:50.260 --> 00:18:53.280
You must know the answer before you're allowed to ask the question.

163
00:18:53.940 --> 00:19:01.160
This is how science works on your planet, apparently. In two thousand seven, Dendreon showed that its immunotherapy drug

164
00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:04.720
Provenge significantly reduced deaths from prostate cancer.

165
00:19:05.800 --> 00:19:10.020
The F.D.A. advisory committee agreed it worked. Then the F.D.A.

166
00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:17.800
rejected it anyway. Not because it didn't save lives. Because Dendreon filled out the wrong form about which lives it was

167
00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:22.180
planning to save. "People stopped dying" wasn't good enough.

168
00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:27.020
The paperwork predicting that people would stop dying wasn't filed in the right order.

169
00:19:27.740 --> 00:19:34.460
Three more years and another trial were required. During those three years, people who could have stopped dying continued

170
00:19:34.460 --> 00:19:41.820
dying, but at least the forms were correct. Due to these additional costs, Dendreon ultimately filed for chapter eleven

171
00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:49.580
bankruptcy. Small Trials Are Dangerous. Phase Three trials test one thousand to three thousand patients.

172
00:19:50.360 --> 00:19:55.960
A one-in-ten-thousand adverse event is mathematically invisible in a trial of three thousand.

173
00:19:56.680 --> 00:20:04.800
Then the drug goes to millions. After approval, the F.D.A. monitors safety using FAERS, a system where doctors voluntarily

174
00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:11.220
report problems if they feel like it. It captures less than ten percent of actual adverse events.

175
00:20:12.120 --> 00:20:19.160
Vioxx killed an estimated thirty-eight thousand to fifty-five thousand Americans before this honor system noticed.

176
00:20:20.040 --> 00:20:26.920
That's more people than died in the entire Korean War, detected by a system that relies on doctors filling out optional

177
00:20:26.920 --> 00:20:36.160
paperwork. A D.F.D.A. (a decentralized F.D.A.) with ten million participants catches one-in-ten-thousand reactions, includes

178
00:20:36.160 --> 00:20:43.380
real populations, tracks long-term outcomes, and provides automated surveillance instead of voluntary paperwork.

179
00:20:44.320 --> 00:20:49.020
You have a fax machine and a suggestion box. One of these is a safety system.

180
00:20:49.640 --> 00:20:55.520
The other is a prayer with an eight-year waiting period. The Negative Results Black Hole.

181
00:20:56.580 --> 00:21:04.040
Here's something that would be illegal if anybody important cared: Negative trial results published: thirty-seven percent.

182
00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:12.080
Positive trial results published: ninety-four percent. Money wasted repeating failed experiments: approximately one hundred

183
00:21:12.080 --> 00:21:18.700
billion dollars annually. Companies are allowed to hide when drugs don't work, which is like letting restaurants hide their

184
00:21:18.700 --> 00:21:22.080
health inspection failures. Actually, restaurants can't do that.

185
00:21:22.820 --> 00:21:27.780
Drugs get less transparency than a sandwich shop. Company: "We tested this drug!".

186
00:21:28.300 --> 00:21:31.860
Regulator: "Did it work?". Company: "...We tested this drug!".

187
00:21:32.720 --> 00:21:36.540
Pharmaceutical companies bury negative results deeper than Jimmy Hoffa.

188
00:21:37.460 --> 00:21:45.040
Other companies waste billions testing the same dead ends. Your insurance premiums fund this magnificent inefficiency.

189
00:21:45.520 --> 00:21:53.900
It's like casinos only having to report when people win. Countries That Don't Have Our "Safety" Japan gives conditional

190
00:21:53.900 --> 00:21:59.770
approval after Phase Two with real-world data collection. Time to patient: two to three years.

191
00:22:00.200 --> 00:22:07.780
Americans fly there for treatment. The E.U. lets terminal patients access experimental drugs at a doctor's discretion.

192
00:22:08.480 --> 00:22:17.240
F.D.A.: "But what if they die?" (They're already dying.). Right to Try (U.S.) passed despite F.D.A.

193
00:22:17.360 --> 00:22:20.960
opposition. The F.D.A. made it effectively impossible to use.

194
00:22:21.500 --> 00:22:26.580
Patients helped: less than two hundred total. Patients who wanted help: tens of thousands.

195
00:22:28.100 --> 00:22:35.780
On Wishonia, "Right to Try" is just called "rights." The fact that your species needed a special law to allow dying people

196
00:22:35.780 --> 00:22:43.280
to take known-safe drugs, and then made the law effectively unusable, is the most human thing I've ever observed.

197
00:22:44.560 --> 00:22:52.000
The COVID Test Fiasco January twenty-twenty: W.H.O. develops COVID test, world starts using it.

198
00:22:52.640 --> 00:22:57.620
February: F.D.A. blocks all non-C.D.C. tests to "ensure quality.".

199
00:22:58.260 --> 00:23:02.660
The C.D.C. tests were contaminated. Private labs begged to help.

200
00:23:03.300 --> 00:23:07.840
Late March: F.D.A. finally allows other tests after thousands die.

201
00:23:08.460 --> 00:23:14.520
The only approved tests didn't work. Ensuring quality control of broken tests is like T.S.A.

202
00:23:14.560 --> 00:23:18.220
confiscating water bottles while letting actual weapons through.

203
00:23:18.780 --> 00:23:26.640
Except people died. The Bottom Line The post-safety efficacy lag is eight point two years.

204
00:23:27.340 --> 00:23:36.220
During that lag, four hundred sixteen million deaths died, seven point nine four billion disability-adjusted life years,

205
00:23:36.540 --> 00:23:44.340
or D.A.L.Y.s, of healthy life were destroyed, and the economic cost reached one point one nine quadrillion dollars.

206
00:23:44.780 --> 00:23:52.180
For every one unit of harm the delay prevented, it created three thousand and seventy units of harm through blocking access.

207
00:23:53.120 --> 00:23:58.520
It is not a safety system. It is a filing system that produces corpses as a byproduct.

208
00:23:59.580 --> 00:24:06.040
The only thing missing is the political will to admit that a law signed before the Beatles existed might not be the pinnacle

209
00:24:06.040 --> 00:24:15.400
of pharmaceutical regulation. Technical Analysis For the full quantitative analysis including methodology, sensitivity analysis,

210
00:24:15.580 --> 00:24:23.120
and source data (warning: contains numbers large enough to make you physically ill), see: The Human Cost of Regulatory Latency.

211
00:24:24.180 --> 00:24:31.340
